{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `obs`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: the indexed likelihood loop `obs[i] ~ poisson_log(...)` was replaced by a deterministic model-local vector `log_lambda_obs` followed by a single plain top-level protected observation statement `obs ~ poisson_log(log_lambda_obs)`. This preserves the same product Poisson-log likelihood while satisfying SafeStan's requirement that protected data be observed exactly once outside loops. Explicit `uniform(0, 5)` and `uniform(0, 3)` priors were added for `sd_alpha` and `sd_eps`, respectively, matching their finite bounded supports and replacing the original implicit uniform priors. The prior order was chosen so parameters are not used before their own prior statements. No data fields were added or changed.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> nobs; // Number of observed data
  int<lower=0> nmis; // Number of missing data
  int<lower=0> nyear; // Number of years
  int<lower=0> nsite; // Number of sites
  array[nobs] int<lower=0> obs; // Observed counts
  array[nobs] int<lower=0> obsyear; // Years in observed data
  array[nobs] int<lower=0> obssite; // Sites in observed data
  array[nmis] int<lower=0> misyear; // Years in missing data
  array[nmis] int<lower=0> missite; // Sites in missing data
}
parameters {
  real mu; // Grand mean
  vector[nsite] alpha; // Random site effects
  real<lower=0, upper=5> sd_alpha;
  vector[nyear] eps; // Random year effects
  real<lower=0, upper=3> sd_eps;
}
transformed parameters {
  matrix[nyear, nsite] log_lambda;

  log_lambda = mu + rep_matrix(alpha', nyear) + rep_matrix(eps, nsite);
}
model {
  vector[nobs] log_lambda_obs;

  // Priors
  mu ~ normal(0, 10);
  sd_alpha ~ uniform(0, 5);
  alpha ~ normal(0, sd_alpha);
  sd_eps ~ uniform(0, 3);
  eps ~ normal(0, sd_eps);

  // Likelihood
  for (i in 1 : nobs) {
    log_lambda_obs[i] = log_lambda[obsyear[i], obssite[i]];
  }
  obs ~ poisson_log(log_lambda_obs);
}
generated quantities {
  array[nmis] int<lower=0> mis;

  for (i in 1 : nmis) {
    mis[i] = poisson_log_rng(log_lambda[misyear[i], missite[i]]);
  }
}
","data_safe_json":"{"missite":[4,1,2],"misyear":[1,1,4],"nmis":3,"nobs":1,"nsite":3,"nyear":1,"obs":[3],"obssite":[4],"obsyear":[4]}","protected_variables":["obs"]}
